<item><title>Burundi researcher explains how earthworms turn farm waste into compost</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-researcher-explains-how-earthworms-turn-farm-waste-417dff/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-researcher-explains-how-earthworms-turn-farm-waste-417dff/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Eric Kazitsa says the process uses agricultural and food-processing residues, with earthworms producing more than 20 offspring monthly when well raised.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:59:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
